@namespace DotNetCloud.Modules.Photos.UI

@*
    Help content for the Photos module.
*@

<div class="help-content">
    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Overview</h2>
        <p>DotNetCloud Photos lets you browse, organize, view, and share your photos in a gallery interface with albums, favorites, a timeline, and a map of geotagged photos.</p>
        <p>Photos are indexed from your Files library rather than uploaded directly. Set up library sources under <strong>Library Settings</strong> and scan to import your images.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Adding Photos</h2>
        <p>Open <strong>Library Settings</strong> in the sidebar, click <strong>Add Source…</strong>, choose one or more folders from your Files library (admin shared folders mounted under <code>_DotNetCloud</code> are also supported), and click <strong>Scan Now</strong>. Supported formats include JPEG, PNG, WebP, BMP, TIFF, SVG, and HEIC/HEIF.</p>
        <p>Overlapping folders are deduplicated during scans. You can reset the collection from Library Settings without affecting your actual image files.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Browsing Photos</h2>
        <p><strong>Gallery view:</strong> Browse all your photos in a responsive grid with thumbnails.</p>
        <p><strong>Albums:</strong> Create albums with <strong>New Album</strong> in the sidebar to group photos by event, trip, or category. Open an album to view its photos, and edit its title or description from the album dialog.</p>
        <p><strong>Timeline:</strong> View photos organized chronologically, grouped by date.</p>
        <p><strong>Favorites:</strong> Star photos to view them together in the Favorites section.</p>
        <p><strong>Map:</strong> Photos with GPS location data appear in the Map section, clustered by coordinates.</p>
        <p>Use the toolbar search box to find photos by filename, and switch between grid and list views.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Viewing Photos</h2>
        <p>Click a photo to open the lightbox viewer. Navigate with arrow keys or the on-screen controls, and view details including file name, date, dimensions, file size, and camera/lens settings when available.</p>
        <p><strong>Editing:</strong> Open the edit panel to rotate, flip, adjust brightness/contrast/saturation, or apply sharpen and blur. Changes can be undone, reverted, or saved.</p>
        <p><strong>Slideshow:</strong> Start a fullscreen slideshow that automatically advances through your photos.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Sharing</h2>
        <p>Share individual photos with other users by entering their user ID in the share dialog, and manage your shares from the <strong>Shared</strong> section.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Tips &amp; Tricks</h2>
        <ul class="help-tips">
            <li>Use albums to organize photos from specific events or trips.</li>
            <li>The timeline view is great for finding photos from a particular date range.</li>
            <li>Use the search bar to find photos by filename.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
